; A floor loom. Nothing is drawn: the cloth comes from structure. Thread each end through a
; shaft, tie each treadle to the shafts it lifts, and choose which treadles each pick presses;
; the cloth re-weaves as you edit. Space throws the shuttle and beats in the next pick from the
; treadling, wrapping when it runs out. Hold the number keys 1–8 while pressing Space to weave
; with those treadles instead, and record them into the treadling. Backspace unweaves the last
; pick, ⌘Z and ⇧⌘Z undo and redo, ⌘O and ⌘S open and save WIF drafts, and ⌘E exports the
; cloth as a PNG. It needs macOS; it plays its clack and thump when a sound output is present.
(import ./loom-sound)
(import ./loom-window)
(import /gui)
(import /lang/product/mac-app)
(blank)

(main
  (<> MacApp
    (= id "com.yumi.loom")
    (= name "Loom")
  )
  (blank)
  (let sound (use (call LoomSound (call loom-sounds))))
  (blank)
  (<> App
    (<> LoomWindow
      (= sound sound)
    )
  )
)
